2026-11-05T08:23:16.304-08:00 [writer] SENT topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="1747616e-811a-4a53-8100-70ebe515811b" plan=["Confirm the leak by analyzing request headers in network traffic.", "Assess impact on authentication tokens and potential data exposure.", "Implement header removal or secure proxy configuration to prevent leaks."] draft="The vulnerability described (CVE-2023-32681) has a **high severity** as confirmed by the s0036_rel advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-05). This issue occurs in the `requests` library for versions >=2.3.0 but <2.31.0. It specifically leaks the `Proxy-Authorization` header during HTTPS redirects, exposing authentication tokens to the destination server. This leak enables potential unauthorized access to sensitive user credentials and session data.  \n\nThe impact is significant: attackers could intercept tokens via intermediate proxies, leading to session hijacking or data breaches. The fix is to upgrade to `requests>=2.31.0`, which securely handles redirects without leaking this header. No additional mitigation steps are required beyond the version update per the advisory. This vulnerability directly compromises authentication security in proxy chains, justifying the high severity rating. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-05 (s0036_rel id 20078): requests affected >= 2.3.0, < 2.31.0, severity high. CVE-2023-32681: Proxy-Authorization header leaked to the destination server on HTTPS redirects. Fixed in 2.31.0."
